# Everything the build produces or the developer's machine holds.
#
# `COPY . .` in the build stage is what makes this file load-bearing rather than an
# optimisation: without it the image would carry the host's node_modules — built for a
# different platform — over the ones the image just installed, and a stale .next over the
# one it is about to build.
node_modules
.next
out
build

# The one that is a security matter rather than a size one. Next loads a .env in the
# working directory automatically, so a copied .env would bake this machine's real
# Railway credentials into an image layer. Service variables are the only channel.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Test and audit output, none of which the runtime reads.
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
.lighthouseci
.lighthouse-cookie

# History, editor state, and the agent rule files. None of it is read at build or run
# time; .ai/rules alone is over a thousand lines of prose crossing into the context.
.git
.github
.cursor
.ai
*.tsbuildinfo
